# The lifecycle of the Maven service demo in one scratch repository: a pull
# request on branch development, its native merge, the service development
# snapshot dispatched on the merged main, then a signed release request from
# it. The Maven service development workflow is the one development route
# Forgejo has, so the Maven service is the one demo this lane runs; a demo
# without a root Maven application and one container is refused
# (docs/live-campaigns.md, Lifecycle). One line per image builder, since on
# Forgejo the builder is the consumer's CI_IMAGE_BUILDER variable: Buildah on
# the contract's runner that permits user namespaces, or kaniko in the
# campaign's job image, labelled for the consumer trial's layer repository
# the lifecycle runs from. Leave FORGE_CI_LIVE_FORGEJO_IMAGE_BUILDER unset:
# set, it refuses the other builder's line. The visibility is the run's:
# FORGE_CI_LIVE_CONSUMER_VISIBILITY unset or both runs each line public and
# private. Native linux/amd64, and the contract's container/readiness runner
# for either builder, since the service's readiness runs the published image
# with Podman. Prepare with forgejo=<this file> and job-image=java:<reviewed
# local image>; CI_JOB_IMAGE is also the Java image the snapshot builds the
# service with. amd64 runners only for now.
#
#   just campaign-lane <dir> forgejo test/live/campaigns/lifecycle-forgejo.cases
setting admin-lint=false
setting admin-vulnerabilities=false
setting admin-application-tests=false

consumer hello-maven-service lifecycle CI_JOB_IMAGE=@JOB_IMAGE_JAVA CI_IMAGE_BUILDER=buildah RELEASE_PLATFORMS=linux/amd64
consumer hello-maven-service lifecycle CI_JOB_IMAGE=@JOB_IMAGE_JAVA CI_IMAGE_BUILDER=kaniko CI_IMAGE_BUILDER_JOB_IMAGE=@KANIKO_JOB_IMAGE RELEASE_PLATFORMS=linux/amd64
